/-!
# [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] at a sheaf of ideals of finite type

[Stacks, Tag 0A0G] asserts that the derived direct image commutes with derived completion: for a
morphism of ringed sites `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)`, a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` and the ideal
sheaf `ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` that Section 52.7 builds out of it, the canonical map

`(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)`

is invertible for every object `K` of `D(𝒪')`. `PushforwardCommutesCompletionCanonical.lean`
proves exactly that in the regime the source's own proof reduces to — `ℐ` generated by finitely
many **global** sections of `𝒪`. This file performs the source's reduction to that case, so the
statement is proved at the source's own data, a sheaf of ideals of **finite type**, which is only
*locally* generated by finitely many sections.

## The reduction

Four inputs, and nothing else:

* a covering family `{V_i}` of the final object of the target site on whose members `ℐ` is
  generated by finitely many sections
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_coversTop_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`);
* the identity `ℐ'|_{u(V)} = (f')^{-1}(ℐ|_V) · 𝒪_{u(V)}` of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal_inverseImageIdealSheaf`, together with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf_generatedIdealSheaf`, which between them
  put *both* sheaves of ideals of the localized pair in the globally generated form on each
  member of the covering — `V` is terminal in `𝒟/V` and `u(V)` in `𝒞/u(V)`, so a section over a
  member is a global section there;
* the restriction coherence
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized`, which
  identifies the restriction of the comparison map of `f` with the comparison map of the
  localized morphism of [Stacks, Tag 04J0] up to the two comparison maps of [Stacks, Tag 0A0F]
  — invertible at sheaves of ideals of finite type — and [Stacks, Tag 0D6G];
* the locality of invertibility in the derived category of sheaves of modules,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`.

## Main results

In the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`:

* `isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_congr`: the invertibility of the comparison map
  depends only on the two sheaves of ideals and not on how they are presented. Everything else
  the comparison map is built from — the relation of [Stacks, Tag 099J] and the existence of the
  two derived completion functors — is a `Prop`.
* `isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_localized_overIdeal`: **[Stacks, Tag 0A0G] for
  the localized morphism at the source's own pair of sheaves of ideals**, over an object on
  which `ℐ` is globally generated.
* `isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0A0G] in full** — the canonical map is invertible for an arbitrary object of
  `D(𝒪')`, at a sheaf of ideals of finite type and the ideal sheaf Section 52.7 constructs from
  it.

## Implementation notes

The source's hypotheses are a morphism of ringed topoi, a sheaf of ideals of finite type, and
nothing on the object. Here the morphism is one of ringed **sites** — the presentation this
development's derived pullback and direct image are built over — and the finite-type hypothesis
is `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`. Finite type of the second sheaf of ideals is *not* assumed: it
is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf`. The relation of
[Stacks, Tag 099J] between the two sheaves of ideals is likewise proved and not assumed, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushforwardIdealCompatible_inverseImageIdealSheaf`.

The instance binders are of one kind only: sheafification of sheaves of modules, and of sheaves
of commutative rings, exists on the two sites and on all of their slices, and total complexes of
the tensor bifunctor exist there. These are the standing hypotheses of this directory and are
discharged at a ringed space, hence at a scheme. There is no hypothesis on the object, none on
the generating family, and none on countable coproducts in a derived category.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04J0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04J0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D6G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D6G)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

